          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#References"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesAsContinuousRealCohomology"} As continuous-real cohomology
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_rationalization_followed_by_extension_of_scalars"} As rationalization followed by extension of scalars
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In analogy to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            %em real homotopy theory
            is to study those aspects of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            that are visible when the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+ring"} ground ring
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} groups
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product
            of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            with the additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+theory"} differential cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in order to connect to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complexes"} de Rham complexes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
          %p
            But a technical issue with generalizing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+dg-algebraic+rational+homotopy+theory"} fundamental theorem of dg-algebraic rational homotopy theory
            to the case of real homotopy theory is that the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PL+de+Rham+complex"} PL de Rham
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction+between+simplicial+sets+and+connective+dgc-algebras"} Quillen adjunction between simplicial sets and connective dgc-algebras
            – which does exist over any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
            and relates to the one over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
            (all reviewed in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FSS20"} FSS 2020, Sec. 3.2
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            only for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{Q}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            – then:
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
          %p
            From the point of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "core+of+a+ring#NoOtherCharZeroFieldIsSolid"} this Remark
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            are not
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+rings"} solid rings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℤ
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} k
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            are not, in general,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to each other, for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \neq \mathbb{Q}
          %p
            On the other hand, from the point of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            the issue is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{R}
            are naturally a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+ring"} topological ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction+between+simplicial+sets+and+connective+dgc-algebras"} Quillen adjunction between simplicial sets and connective dgc-algebras
            over the real numbers.
          %p
            Therefore, the
            %em real homotopy theory
            of
            %a{:href => "#BrownSzczarba95"} Brown &amp; Szczarba 1995
            replaces, in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+dg-algebraic+rational+homotopy+theory"} fundamental theorem of dg-algebraic rational homotopy theory
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+cohomology"} continuous cohomology
            and plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgc-algebras"} dgc-algebras
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+ring"} topological algebras
          %blockquote
            %p
              The authors of (
              %a{:href => "#BrownSzczarba95"}> Brown-Szczarba 95
              ) show how the Bousfield-Gugenheim approach to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              may be extended to the framework of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+cohomology"} continuous cohomology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rationals
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} reals
              has always been effected by a formal tensoring with the reals. While this allows a connection to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham theory
              = succeed "-like" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower"} Postnikov tower
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              (as an
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#BrownSzczarba95"} Brown-Szczarba 95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+models"} minimal models
              which incorporates the usual topology of the reals and a generalization of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/van+Est%27s+theorem"} van Est's theorem
              saying that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ;
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^*(K(\mathbb{R},n); \mathbb{R})
              is a freely generated algebra on one generator (a result which is not true in the discrete topology case). By using the natural topology of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+cohomology"} continuous cohomology
              and applications such as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+classes"} characteristic classes
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliations"} foliations
            %p
              (from the
              %a{:href => "http://mirrors.library.cornell.edu/ZMATH/zmath/en/zmath/search/?an=0865.55009"} Zentralblatt review
              of (
              %a{:href => "#BrownSzczarba95"}> Brown-Szczarba 95
              ))
          %p#RelationToSchematicHomotopyType
            If one thinks of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+topological+spaces"} simplicial topological spaces
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
            on (some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            version of)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} hence
            as presentations for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+infinity-stack"}
                topological
                = succeed "-stacks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schematic+homotopy+types"} schematic homotopy types
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "schematic+homotopy+type#Toen06"} Toën 2006
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topological+infinity-groupoid"}
              D-topological
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            (and further to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoids"}
              smooth
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            etc.) along the lines of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "function+algebras+on+infinity-stacks#Stel"} Stel 2010
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+homotopy+theory"} p-adic homotopy theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schematic+homotopy+type"} schematic homotopy type
          %h2#References References
          %h3#ReferencesAsContinuousRealCohomology As continuous-real cohomology
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+homotopy+theory"} real homotopy theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            over the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+cohomology"} continuous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+algebra"} topological
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgc-algebras"} dgc-algebras
          %ul
            %li#BrownSzczarba95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edgar+Brown"}> Edgar Brown
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+H.+Szczarba"} Robert H. Szczarba
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Real and Rational Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-044481779-2/50018-3"} doi:10.1016/B978-044481779-2/50018-3
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://mirrors.library.cornell.edu/ZMATH/zmath/en/zmath/search/?an=0865.55009"} ZB
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (also introducing
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel-equivariant+rational+homotopy+theory"} Borel-equivariant rational homotopy theory
          %p
            with emphasis on globally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan fibrant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+topological+spaces"} simplicial topological spaces
            (such as
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+topological+groups"} simplicial topological groups
          %ul
            %li#BrownSzczarba89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edgar+H.+Brown"}> Edgar H. Brown
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+H.+Szczarba"} Robert H. Szczarba
              = succeed "," do
                %em Continuous cohomology and real homotopy type
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-1989-0929667-6"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9947-1989-0929667-6
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2001017"} jstor:2001017
          %p
            with arbitrary
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
          %ul
            %li#BrownSzczarba90
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edgar+Brown"}> Edgar Brown
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+H.+Szczarba"} Robert H. Szczarba
                %em Continuous cohomology and Real homotopy type II
                Asterisque 191, Societe Mathematique De France (1990) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/book-part/AST_1990__191__45_0"}> numdam:AST_1990__191__45_0
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edgar+Brown"}> Edgar Brown
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+H.+Szczarba"} Robert H. Szczarba
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Real and rational homotopy theory for spaces with arbitrary fundamental group
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/duke-mathematical-journal/volume-71/issue-1/Rational-and-real-homotopy-theory-with-arbitrary-fundamental-groups/10.1215/S0012-7094-93-07111-6.short"} doi:10.1215/S0012-7094-93-07111-6
          %h3#as_rationalization_followed_by_extension_of_scalars As rationalization followed by extension of scalars
          %p
            Discussion of the plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction+between+simplicial+sets+and+connective+dgc-algebras"} Quillen adjunction between simplicial sets and connective dgc-algebras
            over the real numbers, and its relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            followed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
          %ul
            %li#FSS20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+Character+Map+in+Twisted+Non-Abelian+Cohomology"} The Character Map in Nonabelian Cohomology — Twisted, Differential, Generalizaed
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.11909"} arXiv:2009.11909
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/13422"} doi:10.1142/13422
          %p following
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phillip+Griffiths"} Phillip Griffiths
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"} Dennis Sullivan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Real homotopy theory of Kähler manifolds
              %strong 29
              (1975) 245-274 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01389853"}> doi:10.1007/BF01389853
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            For discussion with focus on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariants"} Hopf invariants
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+integral+formula"} Whitehead integral formula
            see the references
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "Hopf+invariant#ReferencesWhiteheadIntegralFormula"}> there
              \.
